# Frozen 2026-09-15, the run that first turned --ratchets on in this repo.
# Format: <file>	<first comment line, truncated to 60 chars>. Two-way rule: a
# block that is not here FAILS, and a row whose block is gone or has shrunk under
# the limit FAILS too, so the freeze cannot rot. Shrink a block, then DELETE its
# line. third_party/ANTfrastructure/docs/code-quality-tooling.md
#
# WHY THESE ARE FROZEN AND NOT SHORTENED. Every one is a WRAPPER header, and the
# thing it records is why the wrapper is thin: which half of the job moved
# upstream, which knob the hub reads, and which incident the local half exists
# for. The owner directive says long text belongs in docs/ with a pointer, and
# this repo has no docs/*.md to point at - docs/ here is Sphinx sources plus
# generated output (AGENTS.md section 6). Creating a docs page per wrapper is a
# separate decision from turning the ratchet on, so the state is recorded rather
# than churned. The gate now refuses the NEXT one.
#
# scripts/linux/lib/antfrastructure.sh is a vendored copy of the hub's
# shared/linux/templates/antfrastructure.sh and is watched by the shared-config
# drift gate: its blocks can only shrink upstream.
scripts/linux/ci-build-and-test.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/ci-common.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/ci-docs.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/ci-finalize.sh	# Hand the docs tree back to whoever owns the bind mount. Th
scripts/linux/ci-profile-bench.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/ci-release.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/ci-run-all.sh	# clang links against the image's source-built GCC, and BOTH
scripts/linux/lib/antfrastructure.sh	# Replace this process with a ANTfrastructure driver, forwar
scripts/linux/renovate-local.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/run-lint-gates.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
scripts/linux/run-static-analysis-format.sh	# cmake-format lives in a Python env; the library bootstraps
scripts/linux/run-static-analysis-format.sh	#!/usr/bin/env bash
